# Trigger file for the Send Invites workflow.
#
# To fire a send via GitHub Actions:
#   1. Copy this file to `pending-send.url` (same directory).
#   2. Replace the URL placeholder below with a fresh one-time-secret URL
#      whose payload contains:
#         GMAIL_USER=<sender>@gmail.com
#         GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=<16-char app password>
#      (See INVITATION EMAIL/HOW_TO_AUTH.md for how to generate that.)
#   3. Edit the other keys to point at the right campaign body / recipients
#      / from-name. The values below are pre-filled for the Programadores
#      Cariocas survey PILOT (6 test addresses already in mailer/recipients.txt).
#   4. `git add -- 'INVITATION EMAIL/mailer/pending-send.url'`
#      `git commit -m 'send-invites: trigger <campaign>'`
#      `git push`
#   5. The workflow self-triggers on push to `pending-send.url`. After it
#      runs, the trigger file is auto-deleted and the result is committed
#      to `mailer/last-run-status.md`.
#
# Recognized keys (all key=value, one per line, # for comments):
#   url=        REQUIRED. The one-time-secret URL with the Gmail creds.
#   template=   Path to the email body (defaults to mailer/invite_template.txt).
#   recipients= Path to the recipients file (defaults to mailer/recipients.txt).
#               MUST be a path in the repo — gitignored files (e.g. *.local.txt)
#               are NOT in the runner's checkout.
#   from_name=  From display name, e.g. "Equipe Programadores Cariocas".
#   subject=    Override the subject line from the template.

url=https://us.onetimesecret.com/secret/REPLACE_WITH_FRESH_URL
template=INVITATION EMAIL/campaigns/programadores-cariocas-survey/invite_body.txt
from_name=Equipe Programadores Cariocas
